`a voluntary dissolution approved` MEANS `A dissolution` WITH
    `the enterprise asked voluntarily` IS TRUE
    `the term of operation in the licence has ended` IS FALSE
    `the licence was revoked under Dieu 75(1)(a), (b), (d) or (e)` IS FALSE
    `a foreign branch did not restore the ratio after the period of control` IS FALSE
    `another case the law provides` IS FALSE
    `the Ministry of Finance approved in writing` IS TRUE
`a voluntary dissolution not approved` MEANS `A dissolution` WITH
    `the enterprise asked voluntarily` IS TRUE
    `the term of operation in the licence has ended` IS FALSE
    `the licence was revoked under Dieu 75(1)(a), (b), (d) or (e)` IS FALSE
    `a foreign branch did not restore the ratio after the period of control` IS FALSE
    `another case the law provides` IS FALSE
    `the Ministry of Finance approved in writing` IS FALSE
`a term ended` MEANS `A dissolution` WITH
    `the enterprise asked voluntarily` IS FALSE
    `the term of operation in the licence has ended` IS TRUE
    `the licence was revoked under Dieu 75(1)(a), (b), (d) or (e)` IS FALSE
    `a foreign branch did not restore the ratio after the period of control` IS FALSE
    `another case the law provides` IS FALSE
    `the Ministry of Finance approved in writing` IS TRUE
`a revocation` MEANS `A dissolution` WITH
    `the enterprise asked voluntarily` IS FALSE
    `the term of operation in the licence has ended` IS FALSE
    `the licence was revoked under Dieu 75(1)(a), (b), (d) or (e)` IS TRUE
    `a foreign branch did not restore the ratio after the period of control` IS FALSE
    `another case the law provides` IS FALSE
    `the Ministry of Finance approved in writing` IS TRUE
`a branch that did not restore the ratio` MEANS `A dissolution` WITH
    `the enterprise asked voluntarily` IS FALSE
    `the term of operation in the licence has ended` IS FALSE
    `the licence was revoked under Dieu 75(1)(a), (b), (d) or (e)` IS FALSE
    `a foreign branch did not restore the ratio after the period of control` IS TRUE
    `another case the law provides` IS FALSE
    `the Ministry of Finance approved in writing` IS TRUE
`no ground, approval given` MEANS `A dissolution` WITH
    `the enterprise asked voluntarily` IS FALSE
    `the term of operation in the licence has ended` IS FALSE
    `the licence was revoked under Dieu 75(1)(a), (b), (d) or (e)` IS FALSE
    `a foreign branch did not restore the ratio after the period of control` IS FALSE
    `another case the law provides` IS FALSE
    `the Ministry of Finance approved in writing` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `Dieu 115(2): the dissolution or ending may go ahead` `a voluntary dissolution approved`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 115(2): the dissolution or ending may go ahead` `a voluntary dissolution not approved`
#ASSERT `Dieu 115(1): a ground for dissolving the insurer or ending the foreign branch exists` `a term ended`
